nfernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T15:19:37-08:00","id":63148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/58690-changing-breeds-mythos-help?p=58904#post58904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have hyena shifters listed in the skin changers book, but they are considered Uratha, and are in fact werewolves that gained the ability to breed with hyenas and take on a similar form. Still part of the people though. As for the other breeds, they have examples in the back of war against the pure.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are in fact several versions. There are:<br /> 1. Riantes (Laughing Ones) from Changing Breeds. I like to think they never existed, though, while I think others wished the whole book itself didn't exist.<br /> 2. Bouda from Skinchangers. Which are actually Spirit Claimed.<br /> 3. War Against the Pure has a small part that talks about a shapechanging albino female hyena in the Wayward Sons chapter.<br /> 4. The Uratha described in &quot;The Rage&quot; as you stated, you just got the book wrong. And nothing is said about them breeding with hyenas at all, only that they take coloration of the local predators, like Hunting Dogs and jackals. It says only &quot;some&quot; Uratha resemble hyenas in coat coloration. And even then, I think it wouldn't be exact. Like some only have the muzzle and eyes coloration, but no spots, or others only have the spots and lack everything else.<br /> <br /> I do agree with MrParaduo putting shapechanging hyenas under Helios.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;In East Africa, Tabwa mythology portrays the spotted hyena as a solar animal that first brought the sun to warm the cold earth&quot; - from <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyena\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia</a> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 02-01-2014, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theony