,{"date":"2014-05-05T02:44:30-07:00","id":125662,"title":"","content":"Hmh, first of all, I really think that the one thing most NEw World of Darkness games did well was NOT to have a universal creation myth.<br /> Just look at it from a real world perspective:<br /> If you have very diverse sets of shapechangers, who are from different parts of the world and may very well even be opponents or at least not culturally tied together why should they agree on a story of how they or the world or anything came to be?<br /> Why not let them all have their own, different stories, and not even one same one for one breed?<br /> That is how real life works. I think especially our rather unified (rather though, there are enough different faction there too) christian faith blinds us to that quite often.<br /> <br /> So, I would not write a bible of changing breeds for such a line, I would instead make sure they feel like the legends they are supposed to reflect.<br /> <br /> <br /> That aside,well, I hope Changing Breeds will be a line apart from werewolf.<br /> I used to hope differently, but the way werewolf is now developing, I just think other werecreatures will fare better on their own.<br /> Further, a more pluralistic approach may even make it an attractive alternative to have &quot;changing breed werewolves&quot;, similar to how Hunter has rules to run various supernatural creatures without forcing you to use the other game lines.<br /> <br /> I think what changing breeds really would need is:<br /> 1. A connecting element, or why all those different shapeshifters are in one gameline why they would play together and what their enemies would be.<br /> 2. A simple enough mechanic that focuses on the essential and leaves room for each breed to be a bit different without making them too much a special snowflake<br /> 3. Lots of tie ins to real life shapeshifter myths, including different origins maybe (cursed, the result of magic, &quot;divine&quot; blood, etc.)<br /> <br /> Changing Breeds tried to play man VS nature as the underlying theme, I think that was a bad choice. The initial fervour of the movements and ideologies that sprang that kind of thinking just is not what it was once, people on both sides of the debate became more rational and thus, humanity and its industry and pollution do not make a good villain anymore, if they ever did.<br /> I think you can still play up the issue of coexistence, not just man and beast but also different breeds among each other.<br /> One could even make he conflict of man and nature still relevant if it was about a broader theme of preserving balance (which I think has been suggested in previous new changing breed topics).<br /> Enemies then could be both those who despoil and those who try to purge those by destroying all.<br /> Werewolf takes the balance between the material world and the shadow as its main theme, so,why not the balance between man and nature?<br /> Spirits could play a big part in it, but the focus would be more about balancing out the sides, between man made &quot;gods&quot; and nature's avatars who might be as destructive as a volcano or a flood.<br /> That would even eave a lot of conflict between werewolves and other shapeshifters, who might unbalance the shadow in order to rebalance what they see as important.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, I think Changing Breeds should still have aspects, but very, very carefully reworked, but Harmony like the Idigam chronicles, maybe their own brand of Rite / magic and, hopefully, a better shifting system.<br /> I think the idea of only a certain number of forms was good /trims the ballast and make sit closer to many legends) but the stats should follow a good formula and, frankly, I would prefer Death Rage and War Form to be a bit less universal.<br /> For example, looking at how vampire has frenzy and riding the wave, why not make instead &quot;animal instincts&quot;, which can be both beneficial or a hindrance (like flight instinct helping you perceive dangers but also making it so that you can more easily be spooked and might flee when things turn badly) and working the war form / death rage mechanic into one of those? A fighting instinct that gives you some of the boni of a Gauru form, but at the price of risking death rage?<br /> This would also allow one to make less combat orientated breeds who lack those rather juciy boni in a fight but also won't risk going berserk (but likely risking flight in return).<br /> <br /> A, I might have ended up digressing quite a bit, but, umh, really, for a mythos, I can only repeat, be very careful with the universal mythos, especially in a game full of diverse characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T05:30:25-07:00","id":125734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ray White</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/58690-changing-breeds-mythos-help?p=125662#post125662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmh, first of all, I really think that the one thing most NEw World of Darkness games did well was NOT to have a universal creation myth.<br /> Just look at it from a real world perspective:<br /> If you have very divers