th rage?<br /> This would also allow one to make less combat orientated breeds who lack those rather juciy boni in a fight but also won't risk going berserk (but likely risking flight in return).<br /> <br /> A, I might have ended up digressing quite a bit, but, umh, really, for a mythos, I can only repeat, be very careful with the universal mythos, especially in a game full of diverse characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>You, sir, are a saint. Thank you for saving me from going overboard with this. I can see the logic of your statement, and am ever grateful for it. :3<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T09:01:40-07:00","id":125844,"title":"","content":"Hmh, this reminds me, did you see this thread form a while ago?^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33067-ancients-awaken-the-old-ones-chronicles-changing-breeds-discussion-brainstorming\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33067-ancients-awaken-the-old-ones-chronicles-changing-breeds-discussion-brainstorming\"> Ancients Awaken- the Old Ones Chronicles (Changing Breeds. Discussion, Brainstorming) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33067-ancients-awaken-the-old-ones-chronicles-changing-breeds-discussion-brainstorming\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33067-ancients-awaken-the-old-ones-chronicles-changing-breeds-discussion-brainstorming </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> In a way, this is the most ambitious project of mine among the Weekly Projects, for it require to analyze the Changing Breeds and rework them, from fluff to mechanics and make sure that everything works ok. My idea is to take the Eco-terrorists which are presented in the book and make them into something.. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I have not fully read it all, but I start to think it might be really neat to have all the people interested in a new and better Changing breed get together and do something.^^<br /> Then we could even try and see if Onyx Path would like to publish it.^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T12:13:53-07:00","id":126031,"title":"","content":"Nice! Looks very promising, I have to admit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T03:45:30-07:00","id":126587,"title":"","content":"It certainly does look like there are a good number of different opinions on how it should look...^^<br /> <br /> Which of course is understandable, just, I realy think it would be great if with all those people talking about why changing breeds was bad and needs to be made anew to be something fun, it is a shame nothing yet has come of it.<br /> I really think there would be a market for a game of shapeshifters that is not just werewolf.<br /> People like animals, there are a lot of stories, especially for a younger audience, that feature a animal / totem or shapeshifting theme heavily and while most world of darkness lines have a niche for the shapeshifter and animal speaker, it should be able to stand on its own, after all, many gamelines have niches for the one doing strange rituals and similarr and we still get Mage (and qutie a few games have aspects of lifestealing too).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T06:16:06-07:00","id":126657,"title":"","content":"I think people often forget that humans are also animals, technically speaking. We're a part of nature, even if sometimes self-destructive. Just as the termite creates mounds out of earth and labor, we've built towns and structures of stone and glass. Perhaps its because of how much influence we have over the mundane that, in a game like this, spirits would see it useful to treat human shapechangers as mediators between both worlds. Not because we're special, but because it's tactical, given the current situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 05-06-2014, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T09:35:58-07:00","id":126756,"title":"","content":"Personally, for 'lesser' Changing Breeds, I'm going to use the rues for Wolf-Blooded, probably add in a coupe of different Tells, and use those as the basis (maybe allowing them to have 2 Tells each)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T13:55:22-07:00","id":126938,"title":"","content":"Hmh, I have not et read the teaser about the wolfblooded, but it does sound like they made them much more fun already...^^<br /> <br /> I actually was thinking, if Changing Breeds gets a make over, then Skin Thieves should be their &quot;lesser template&quot;.<br /> They already share mechanics similar to how ghouls use disciplines...<br /> <br /> I did pm the creator of the linked thread today and I think maybe it would really be good if we tried to pull our lot together.<br /> <br /> See, we all have our own ideas, but like vampire managed to be even more inclusive with the revenants, posthumous embraces and the banes you can acquire at low humanity or the stryx as opponents, I think the changing breeds that should be is the one where all those ideas WORK in the same line.<br /> Like in vampire the covenants often have their own legends about how vampires (or at least one vampire with the ordo dracul) came to be, we could also have different legends in a changing breeds game, we can have a lot of things and they do not need to be exclusive of others either.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T05:34:41-07:00","id":127403,"title":"","content":"Totally missed the thread's purpose and thus I have edited this post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}